Algorithm:

Step 1: Sort the given array so that duplicate elements come together.
Step 2: Create a list to store all unique subsets.
Step 3: Start a recursive process with an empty subset and starting index 0.
Step 4: At each recursive call, check if the current subset is already present in the result list.
Step 5: If it is not present, add the current subset to the result list.
Step 6: Traverse the array from the current starting index to the end.
Step 7: Include the current element in the subset.
Step 8: Recursively continue the process with the next index to explore further subsets.
Step 9: After returning from recursion, remove the last element to backtrack and try other combinations.
Step 10: Continue this process until all elements are processed and all unique subsets are generated.

Time Complexity: O(2ⁿ × n)
Space Complexity: O(n) 


-----> Code <-----

class Solution {
    public List<List<Integer>> subsetsWithDup(int[] nums) {
        List<List<Integer>> ans=new ArrayList<>();
        List<Integer> al=new ArrayList<>();
        Arrays.sort(nums);
        func(nums,ans,al, 0);
        return ans;
    }
    public static void func(int[] nums,List<List<Integer>> ans,List<Integer> al,int st){
        if(al.size()<=nums.length && !ans.contains(al)){
            ans.add(new ArrayList<>(al));
        }
        for(int i=st;i<nums.length;i++){
            al.add(nums[i]);
            func(nums,ans,al,i+1);
            al.remove(al.size()-1);
        }
    }
}
